---
date: 2026-06-05T16:40:21-04:00
---

The Magical Crimes Convox is a department within the [[Org/Iridescent Church/index|Iridescent Church]] devoted to solving the unexplained and the weird when they negatively impact the [[Iridescent Host|Host's]] people. Some cases they've worked on previously have included a mysterious curse originating from the [[Verdant Expanse]] and an everlasting rain from excessive [[Phenomena/Augury|augury]].

The convox is headquartered at 33 Rook's Crossing in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Aurideon/index|Aurideon]].

Its deputy director is Major-Chaplain [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Ewan McFoster|Ewan McFoster]]. He speaks for the convox in public, and during the endless rain over [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] he went on [[The Situation Room|the radio]] to say the weather was the work of an illegal augur and that the convox was giving all its resources to the hunt.

The convox sent three of its members to [[Geography/Calaria/Wrenford|Wrenford]] to trace a killer who left forty-eight dead in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]], dried to husks in their beds: [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Mickey Ironroots|Mickey Ironroots]], [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Cedric Corot|Cedric Corot]], and [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Magical Crimes/People/Krod Snodman|Krod Snodman]]. The Church reimburses the travel of its investigators.

The three investigators followed the curse into the [[Verdant Expanse]]. There they met a [[Bestiary/Verdant Court Fey|court of fey]], refused its offer to end the curse at the price of entering their Lady's court, and killed the court's leaders. The curse continued, and another person died while they returned to [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] to report.

With the case still open, the three took their one remaining lead, the stone necklace taken from [[People/Lyric Burke|Lyric Burke]]'s house, to [[Org/Crystal's Rock|Crystal's Rock]], a jewelers' conference in Hallia. There they found that [[Phenomena/Feyrock|Feyrock]] is bought and sold only by those wealthy enough to afford it, and that [[Org/Guren and Guren/People/Amos Guren|Amos Guren]] had lately bought a piece from a bandaged man in a black raiment. The lead took them to [[People/Anthony|Anthony]]'s apartment in the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Gullet/index|Gullet]], where they found him dead above a ritual circle and half-turned to stone, and afterward into the [[Phenomena/Gloaming Codex|Gloaming Codex]] itself.
